{
	"contentrating" : "Everyone",
	"description" : "Live kinetic typography for whatever you're playing: Spotify or any media player Wallpaper Engine can see. The lyrics are synced and fly in word by word, styled to match the song.\n\nWHAT IT DOES\n- Synced lyrics, fetched automatically for the song you're playing (LRCLIB and NetEase)\n- 38 layouts and 22 transition styles, chosen per line so a song never looks the same twice\n- Camera modes: Follow (the camera travels across a canvas of lines, now and then diving through the hole of a letter into the next line), Stream (the lyrics run as one continuous path that goes sideways, drops down, spirals onto a flywheel, crescendos and slams), and Auto (mixes them by song section)\n- Light and text that react to the music: bass, kicks and drops\n- Song-structure aware: choruses, verses, bridges and drops each get their own treatment\n- Backgrounds: blurred album art, colour gradient, solid, custom colour, or animated (flowing colours / drifting album art)\n- Multi-monitor layouts, an idle clock when nothing is playing, and an invert option for transparent displays (Lucid Panel)\n- Self-healing: recovers by itself from network drops, lost audio and song changes\n\nSETTINGS WORTH TRYING\n- Camera: Auto / Follow / Stream / Edit moves / Subtle / Off\n- Layout and Transition: leave on Auto/Mixed, or lock one you like\n- Lyrics offset: nudge it if a song's lyrics run early or late, or hover the bottom-right corner for « earlier / later » per song and ⟳ to reload\n- Raise song info: lifts the now-playing card above your taskbar\n\nTIPS\n- On multi-monitor setups, Wallpaper Engine > Settings > Performance > FPS 30 roughly halves the GPU use and still looks smooth\n- Lyrics come from public databases, so a few songs have no synced lyrics; the wallpaper shows the song title instead\n\nMade by Il-Kikkinu. Bugs or ideas? Leave a comment.",
